    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0768" n="736" xml:id="pg736"/>

                <head>300. Memorandum From the Officer in Charge of Cuban Affairs (Hurwitch) to the Assistant
                    Secretary of State for Inter-American Affairs (Woodward)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d300-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-02-01">February 1,
                        1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>“Cuba Project”</item>
                </list>
                <p>Attached for your urgent consideration is the latest version of the basic paper
                    relating to the “Cuban Project.”<anchor n="1" xml:id="d300-f2"/> There is also
                    attached a memorandum to each member of the group from General Lansdale.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d300-f3"
                    /> A number of tasks listed in the basic paper have been assigned to the
                    Department. Although I have done a little preliminary work on some of these
                    tasks, I have been reluctant until now to proceed very far both because of
                    uncertainty as to the final outcome of the Punta del Este meeting and in the
                    absence of your guidance.</p>
                <p>I shall appreciate an early opportunity, in view of the deadlines imposed, to
                    discuss the paper with you and obtain your views as to the best manner of
                    proceeding, particularly with regard to Task #9 (page 5).<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d300-f4"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d300-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d300-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of Stare, Central Files, 737.00/1-2062. Top Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d300-f2" n="1" xml:id="d300-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d291">Document 291</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d300-f3" n="2" xml:id="d300-f3-content">
                <p><ref target="#d293">Document 293</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d300-f4" n="3" xml:id="d300-f4-content">
                <p>Woodward responded, in a handwritten note
                    on the memorandum, directed to Hurwitch
                    and Goodwin: “I believe we can now forge
                    ahead on all items feasibly attainable.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
